  "body": "Closes #1211\nClaim: cloud/i1211-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1211-sonnet)\n\n### Problem\nThe three Réglages sliders (text size, accent hue, dark brightness) lag.\n\n### Cause (from the code; not measured)\nEach tick set the model property directly: hue wrote two store keys and rebuilt both accents (up to 1,000 steps), brightness and text size wrote one key each. Every model change also invalidates the app root (`appTheme`, `textScale`). Instruments is not available from a Linux session, so the per-tick cost is not measured here (see below).\n\n### Change\n- New `SliderDraft`: while a drag is on, the value lives in a `@State` draft; the model/store get the final value once on `onEditingChanged(false)`. A change outside a drag (VoiceOver increment/decrement) is saved at once, each step.\n- `ThemeSettingsView`: hue and brightness sliders, their readouts, and the mode tiles / light / dark previews follow the draft live; the app root follows on release.\n- `SettingsView`: text size slider extracted to `TextSizeRow` (re-render scoped to the row); percentage follows the finger, the app-wide scale changes on release.\n- Hue step left at 0.001: not changed without a measurement.\n- No coalescing timer: release-only is the simpler of the two options in the issue.\n\n### Tests\n`SliderDraftTests` (app tests, cannot run on Linux): 200 drag ticks → 0 store writes, exactly 1 on release; tap without movement → none; steps outside a drag → saved each. Red on today's code: `SliderDraft` does not exist, and a direct model assignment writes per tick.\n\n### Measure on a Mac (owed, #893)\nTime Profiler + SwiftUI instrument, 3 s drag per slider, before/after: main-thread ms/s, root `body` evaluations, store writes, reader script injections. Device check: the three sliders follow the finger.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
