   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, a05b0c0e2fea687b4, round 1)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**, head ae8d89ca5a89bc176128d96815c4a503d4f469b3\n\n1. **Medium**, `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/ThemeSettingsView.swift:21-28` (`previewAppearance`). With the Legacy theme selected, the previews replace the stored accents and brightness even when no drag is in progress. `ThemeSettingsModel.init` keeps `theme_day_color_action` / `theme_night_color_action` as stored (an older version may have set any colour; the night accent is a key of its own). A user with a day accent of saturation 0.3, or a night accent of another hue, sees `dayTint`/`nightTint` of `accentHue` in `ThemeModeTiles`, `LightStylePreview` and `DarkStylePreview` instead of the colours the app uses. Breaks \"behaviour unchanged\". Fix: override accents only when `hueDraft.draft != nil`, and `darkBrightness` only when `brightnessDraft.draft != nil`.\n\n2. **Low**, `SliderDraftTests.swift`. The tests cover only `SliderDraft`; removing the wiring from the three views leaves every test green, so \"a drag writes once\" is never tested on the shipped path. Fix: move the save/`editingChanged` glue into a testable helper shared by the views and test it with `CountingStore`; otherwise say the wiring is checked by hand and add it to #893.\n\n3. **Detail.** If the row disappears while a finger is down (e.g. theme switches away from Legacy), `onEditingChanged(false)` may never fire and the dragged value is dropped silently. Acceptable, but the code should say so.\n\nChecked, nothing to report: `@State` mutation via `mutating` calls in the `Binding`/`onEditingChanged` closures; local `@Bindable` capture in `Binding(set:)` (same pattern as `SecuritySettingsSections.swift:51`); `CountingStore` vs `SettingsStore: Sendable`; test initial state. `swiftlint lint --strict` clean on the 4 files; no build or test run (Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
