   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, a4cc54c52245d5a90, round 2)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**, head 98f4059\n\n1. **High**, `SliderDraftTests.swift:14`: `func editing(_ on: Bool)` breaks `identifier_name` (3 to 40 characters). CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict`, so the SwiftLint check goes red (reproduced by the reviewer). Fix: rename the parameter, e.g. `isOn`.\n2. **Low**, `ThemeSettingsView.swift:89-92,128-132`, `SettingsView.swift:203-207`: nothing is actually shared; each view writes its own `set:` / `onEditingChanged:` closures and the test types its own copy. A view that drops `onEditingChanged:` or saves into the wrong property stays green. Fix: one helper that builds the binding and the editing callback, used by the views; or say the view wiring is only checked by hand on a device (#893).\n\nRound 1 points: previews fixed (override only while that slider has a drag in progress); mid-drag disappearance documented. Compile check by reading: nested `$0` closures, `@State` mutating calls, escaping `@Bindable` capture, `Slider(value:in:step:onEditingChanged:)`, `SettingsStore` conformance all look correct. Verified with `swiftlint lint --strict` at repo level in a throwaway worktree; no build or test run (Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
