   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, af5b13658582bbf59, round 3)**\n\n**APPROVE**, head f6532aa\n\nBoth round 2 findings are fixed; SwiftLint is clean (0 violations in 2838 files); the three sliders share one `DraftSlider`. Nothing new blocks the merge.\n\n1. **Detail**, `ThemeSettingsView.swift:86` and `:119`: after a `DraftSlider(...) { … }` trailing closure, the modifiers start at the call's indent. Compiles and lints; indenting one level would read more clearly. Optional.\n2. **Note**: every head stopped at the macOS draft gate (#477), so the app has never been compiled here. Checked by reading: `@Binding` memberwise init with `$hueDraft`; trailing closure then modifiers; `TextSizeRow` receiving the model from the `@Bindable` local (as `DefaultBrowserRow`); fileprivate init used in the same file; `Binding(get:set:)` capturing a non-Sendable `save` (same as `ComposerEditorCard.swift:76`, `ReplyComposerView.swift:181`). The final macOS run is the proof.\n\nVerified: diff read; `swiftlint lint --strict` clean; `SliderDraft` compiled alone with `swiftc -swift-version 6` and run (drag 0.4 then 0.5 saves nothing until release, then `[0.5]` once; a value after release saves at once); model setters do not re-write an equal value; `init` writes nothing and the default brightness is 1, so the test's `writes == 0` / `== 1` hold; a per-tick save would give 200 writes and fail the test.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
